### Changed

- Integrate the M9 Frontend Redesign and add the v1.9.0 release notes to `main`. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown answers with `AssistantMarkdown.Render(markdown, citations)`, keeping unanchored citations in the sources list. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Make the first actionable suggested ticket step a primary control that runs its mapped action. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable `CommandPalette` to `MainLayout`, with navigation from `NavRegistry` and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Apply ticket status changes optimistically on the board and detail view, reconciling successful board moves and restoring the prior state after rejection. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace `AssignTicketDialog` and `ChangeStatusDialog` with header-anchored `MudMenu` popovers that apply assignment and status changes in place. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges where citation titles match assistant answer text, with a numbered sources list for citations that are not anchored. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Inject the active agent roster into the chat system prompt using `GetAgentsHandler`, and direct the assistant to use only listed names. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Force `AgentLoop` to select `check_grounding` through `tool_choice` when retrieved passages are available and no check has run. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Centralize palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors in `Theme/DesignTokens.cs`, and build `MudTheme` from the same constants. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap the board card title link in `board-card__title-row` so `-webkit-line-clamp` can limit titles to two lines. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Target `.assistant-chat` through `::deep` to restore the panel styles and keep the composer send button inside the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Set the ticket queue's Category column width to 140px so its header no longer overlaps Due. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add chat system-prompt rules requiring tool-confirmed success before claiming a change and avoiding unnecessary confirmation for requested actions. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket summary timestamps to `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` in `BuildTicketPrompt` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Mark caught technical knowledge-base search failures as `IsError: true`, keeping them distinct from unavailable results. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score grounding semantically with `SemanticGroundingEvaluator` and retain `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
